derived_display_label (string)

evidential_anchoring_status (string)

unclassified_reason (string or null)

not_determinable_flag (boolean)

provisional_flag (boolean)

threshold_sensitive_flag (boolean)

regime_not_determinable (boolean)

identity_partition_sensitive (boolean)

created_at (ISO8601)

updated_at (ISO8601)

6.8 Provenance
The provenance table holds the provenance records. Each provenance record has:

provenance_id (string, primary key)

annotation_id (string, foreign key to annotation)

annotator_id (string)

annotator_affiliation (string)

timestamp (ISO8601)

source (string)

tool_version (string)

operation (create, update, delete)

created_at (ISO8601)

6.9 Audit Log
The audit_log table holds the audit log entries. Each audit log entry has:

audit_id (string, primary key)

operation (create, update, delete, query, export, import)

record_type (annotation, node, event, partition, model, revision, domain_annotation)

record_id (string)

annotator_id (string)

timestamp (ISO8601)

result (success, failure)

details (JSON)

created_at (ISO8601)

6.10 Referential Integrity
The database enforces the following referential integrity constraints:

Every annotation.node_id must exist in node_registry.

Every annotation.event_node_id, if not null, must exist in event_registry.

Every annotation.partition_id and annotation.partition_version must exist in partition_registry.

Every annotation.model_id must exist in model_registry.

Every annotation.revision_id must exist in revision_registry.

Every domain_annotation.node_id must exist in node_registry.

Every domain_annotation.partition_id and domain_annotation.partition_version must exist in partition_registry.

Every provenance.annotation_id must exist in annotation.

The revision chain (supersedes and superseded_by) must be acyclic.

6.11 Indexes
The database has indexes on:

node_registry.node_id

node_registry.system_scope, model, granularity

event_registry.event_node_id

partition_registry.partition_id, partition_version

model_registry.model_id

