Validation Engine Design
The database validates the following:

Validation 1. Record validity. Every record is validated against the STAG JSON Schema and the thirty-two semantic rules before it is stored.

Validation 2. Referential integrity. Every foreign key reference must resolve to an existing record.

Validation 3. Supersession acyclicity. The revision chain must be acyclic.

Validation 4. Partition consistency. Every domain annotation must belong to the partition identified by partition_id and partition_version.

Validation 5. Node identity consistency. Every node must have a unique node_id and a consistent tuple (S, M, G).

Validation 6. Provenance completeness. Every record must have a provenance record.

Validation 7. Audit completeness. Every operation must have an audit log entry.

